  "description" : "#### **The Company** We help Australian and US businesses hire high calibre remote talent from Sri Lanka. We are a boutique talent partner that works with a limited number of clients and a highly selective pool of talent. Rather than focusing on volume, we focus on quality and long term partnerships. We build dedicated teams across Finance, Technology and Operations, allowing businesses to scale with exceptional talent at a fraction of local hiring costs. Our consultants work as an extension of your team while we handle recruitment, HR, payroll and compliance. #### **Employment Details** - Employment Type: Long-term Contract - Work Arrangement: Fully Remote / Work from Home - Working Days: Monday to Friday (Weekdays) - Working Hours: Semi-aligned with AEST - Communication: Good English communication skills, both written and verbal #### **The Role** We are looking for a Full Stack Software Engineer to join an Australian client. This is a full-time role, 40 hours per week, and semi-aligned to the Australian time zone. #### **Requirements** - Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related field. - 2+ years experience building full stack applications using React, Next.js, Node.js and TypeScript. - Experience working with Large Language Models (LLMs) such as OpenAI, Anthropic, Gemini, or similar AI platforms. - Experience building AI powered applications, chatbots, AI agents, automations, or workflow solutions. - Experience working with PostgreSQL, MySQL, MongoDB, or similar databases. - Understanding of REST APIs, webhooks, third party integrations, and modern software architecture. - Experience with cloud platforms such as AWS, GCP, Vercel, Railway, or similar. - Experience with prompt engineering, AI model integrations, and Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG). - Strong English communication skills. #### **Responsibilities** - Design, develop, and maintain AI-powered web applications. - Build scalable frontend applications